      "writtenOn": "2023-11-22T22:57:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, daisydog runs in user space. When it hangs, there is a chance that the kernel is still functioning. Don\u0027t we want to give the kernel a chance to collect some logs? How do we ensure we\u0027re not over-reacting?",
      "parentUuid": "72c30935_f0e54dbb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "03d61b6644ea1ceb8a4dcf549f1cb456237e0f60",
