        "uuid": "06cd7024_f33e60ea",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1442602
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-24T12:03:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The user app only loop and write a dummy value to `/dev/watchdog` in case of crash the system cleans up the process in terms closing open files descriptors - e.g. `/dev/watchdog\u0027 and that in turn stops the watchdog.\nThe default timeout is set to 30 seconds, but the daisydog is set to pet the watchdog every 2s, so if there is no such an event and the descriptors were not closed it is likely we are in trouble.\n\nThe kernel watchdog is a generic API, the daisydog this way is used in other chromebooks as well.",
      "parentUuid": "f9cdef81_6ec18c40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "03d61b6644ea1ceb8a4dcf549f1cb456237e0f60",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
