      "writtenOn": "2023-11-22T12:22:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no reason to send any events as AP is hang. The original code was doing it, but it was a dead code - there was/is no code that was waiting for it or processing it. In current approach it is also not needed.\nWhen kernel boots, it calls daisydog with `-c` flag which in turn will ask EC (via `/dev/watchdog` and kernel module) if this is a clear boot or EC detected a hang and rebooted AP. This information is logged in `/var/log/messages` and also UMA stats are send (please check: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/daisydog)",
      "parentUuid": "f2a0f6c2_d135c56a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
